    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for offensive momentum today, headlined by a high-efficiency core led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Andy Pages** (71.11). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits tremendously from a favorable matchup against Chandler (4.92 xERA), with dynamic platoon advantages contributing to a +14% boost that solidifies his role as our primary middle-infield spark. Similarly, **Andy Pages** maximizes a soft matchup against the 5.11 xERA of Sears, buoyed by a prime #2 lineup spot that ensures high volume. **Gunnar Henderson** (70.61) remains an elite start despite facing a tougher arm in Lodolo; his underlying plate discipline and the current lineup construction overcome the platoon disadvantage, making him a cornerstone for runs and HR production.\n\nOur deepest bench decision centered on **Denzer Guzman** (44.33), who was the final omission from the starting nine. While **Denzer Guzman** posted a respectable score above the floor, he lacked the explosive upside of the starting outfield contingent. We prioritized **Heliot Ramos** (59.49) over the bench options because the specific tactical edge of the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which theoretically boosts **Heliot Ramos**'s stolen base probability\u2014adds critical value in our league\u2019s scarcity-driven environment. Meanwhile, **Josh Lowe** (38.64) was correctly sidelined, as his poor lineup positioning and unfavorable platoon split against Suarez pushed him well below our efficiency threshold.\n\nRisks for today\u2019s slate are largely confined to the catcher and depth positions. **Liam Hicks** (41.45) and **Dominic Smith** (43.33) are trending toward our bench floor, largely due to strong opposing starters like Jump and McLean. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** closely, as any further shift in the lineup order would likely trigger a benching to protect our remaining games. We continue to navigate the roster without **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who 